{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Unto Elohim.</b> To a court — he must be judged by those who sold him to him (ibid.)." "<b>Unto the door or unto the doorpost.</b> One might think the doorpost is valid to bore against — Scripture says, ״וְנָתַתָּה בְּאָזְנוֹ וּבַדֶּלֶת״ — in the door and not in the doorpost. If so, what does Scripture tell by ״אוֹ אֶל הַמְּזוּזָה״? It likens the door to the doorpost: just as the doorpost is fixed upright, so the door must be fixed upright (ibid.)." "<b>And his master shall bore his ear through with an awl.</b> The right one, or perhaps not, but the left? Scripture says ״אֹזֶן אֹזֶן״ — a gezerah shavah. It is said here ״וְרָצַע אֲדֹנָיו אֶת אָזְנוֹ״, and it is said of the leper ״תְּנוּךְ אֹזֶן הַמִּטַּהֵר הַיְמָנִית״ (Leviticus 14) — just as there it is the right, so too here the right. And what did the ear see to be bored, more than all other limbs of the body? Rabban Yochanan ben Zakkai said: This ear that heard at Mount Sinai ״לֹא תִגְנֹב״, and went and stole — let it be bored. And if he sold himself — the ear that heard at Mount Sinai ״כִּי לִי בְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל עֲבָדִים״, and went and acquired a master for himself — let it be bored. Rabbi Shimon would expound this verse by way of a fortiori: what distinguishes door and doorpost from all vessels in the house? The Holy One, blessed be He, said: the door and doorpost that were witnesses in Egypt when I passed over the lintel and over the two doorposts and said ״כִּי לִי בְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל עֲבָדִים״ — they are My servants and not servants to servants — and this one went and acquired a master for himself, let him be bored before them (Kiddushin 22)." "<b>And he shall serve him forever.</b> Until the Jubilee — or is it truly forever, as its plain sense? Scripture says ״וְאִישׁ אֶל מִשְׁפַּחְתּוֹ תָּשׁוּבוּ״ (Leviticus 25) — this tells that fifty years are called עוֹלָם. And not that he serves him a full fifty years, but he serves him until the Jubilee — whether close or far off (Kiddushin 15)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:33.210070332Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}